WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.562
Why does this chapter matter?

2
00:00:01.562 --> 00:00:04.062
Because both of its subjects fail quietly.

3
00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:07.623
A tenant policy that someone
set once in the portal can't

4
00:00:07.623 --> 00:00:11.262
be reviewed or compared, so
nobody notices when it drifts.

5
00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:15.862
And a certificate that nobody rotates is
simply an outage waiting for its date.

6
00:00:15.862 --> 00:00:18.865
So the chapter turns the
policy into a reviewed file,

7
00:00:18.865 --> 00:00:23.263
compared with the tenant and applied
through a path that can only tighten it.

8
00:00:23.263 --> 00:00:26.706
And it turns rotation into
a plan: raised early,

9
00:00:26.706 --> 00:00:31.600
approved by an owner, renewed,
overlapped, and only then cleaned up.

10
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.140
Let's see where it runs.
